   "subject": "Re: Failling to plot data matrix with intervals (so not a continuous coloured heatmap) with tree",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Ah super! I thought that the findintervals functions does that, but this solves it als well.<div><br></div><div>Thank you very much</div><div>My best,</div><div>Setareh</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Feb 28, 2018 at 6:37 AM, Yu, Guangchuang <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gc...@connect.hku.hk</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">There is no problems.</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248) none repeat scroll 0% 0%\">gheatmap(Boom,mod_mat,offset=<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">5</span>, width=<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">0.5</span>,colnames_angle=-<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">45</span>,hjust=<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">0</span>)\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">will plot the tree with the heatmap.</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248) none repeat scroll 0% 0%\">gheatmap(Boom,mod_mat,offset=<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">5</span>, width=<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">0.5</span>,colnames_angle=-<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">45</span>,hjust=<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">0</span>)+scale_color_manual(values = c(color_palette, breaks=label_text))\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">You code will produce identical figure (left side of the screenshot below) as <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">scale_color_manual</code> will be ignored.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Actually, you put the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">)</code> in wrong place in <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">scale_color_manual(values = c(color_palette, breaks=label_text))</code>.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">You need to use <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">scale_fill_manual</code>. As showed below on the screenshot, using <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">+scale_fill_manual</code> will throw error as your input matrix is continuous value while you are try to set color as discrete value.</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248) none repeat scroll 0% 0%\">&gt; label_text\r\n [<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>] <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;0&quot;</span>       <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;1&quot;</span>       <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;2&quot;</span>       <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;3&quot;</span>       <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;4&quot;</span>       <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;5&quot;</span>       <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;6-7&quot;</span>\r\n [<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">8</span>] <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;8-10&quot;</span>    <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;11-15&quot;</span>   <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;16-20&quot;</span>   <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;21-25&quot;</span>   <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;26-30&quot;</span>   <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;31-35&quot;</span>   <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;36-40&quot;</span>\r\n[<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">15</span>] <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;41-50&quot;</span>   <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;51-60&quot;</span>   <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;61-70&quot;</span>   <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;71-80&quot;</span>   <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;81-90&quot;</span>   <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;91-100&quot;</span>  <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;101-200&quot;</span>\r\n[<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">22</span>] <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;201-300&quot;</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;&gt;300&quot;</span>\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">How would you expect that <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">ggplot2</code> knows e.g. the number 12 should be put in the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">11-15</code> category?</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">You should first prepare your data to fit the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">break</code> (i.e. <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">label_text</code>) that you want to map with <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">values</code> (i.e. color).</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,248) none repeat scroll 0% 0%\">mod_mat2=cut(mod_mat, c(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">2</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">3</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">4</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">5</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">6</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">8</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">11</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">16</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">21</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">26</span>)) %&gt;% matrix(ncol=ncol(mod_mat))\r\nrownames(mod_mat2) = rownames(mod_mat)\r\ncolnames(mod_mat2) = colnames(mod_mat)\r\n\r\nlabel_text &lt;-  c(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;(0,1]&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;(1,2]&quot;</span>,  <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;(2,3]&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;(3,4]&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;(4,5]&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;(5,6]&quot;</span>, \r\n     <span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;(6,8]&quot;</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;(8,11]&quot;</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;(11,16]&quot;</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;(16,21]&quot;</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;(21,26]&quot;</span>) \r\ngheatmap(Boom,mod_mat2,offset=<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">5</span>, width=<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">0.5</span>,colnames_angle=-<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">45</span>,hjust=<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">0</span>) +\r\n    scale_fill_manual(values = color_palette[<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">11</span>], breaks=label_text)\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/bioc-ggtree/attach/2b632a65f2e0a/Screenshot%202018-02-28%2012.26.39.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" height=\"527\" width=\"518\"><br>​<br>​<br></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdj48ZGl2PlRoZXJlIGlzIG5vIHByb2JsZW1zLjxicj48YnI+PC9kaXY+YGBgcjxicj5naGVh\r\ndG1hcChCb29tLG1vZF9tYXQsb2Zmc2V0PTUsIHdpZHRoPTAuNSxjb2xuYW1lc19hbmdsZT0tNDUs\r\naGp1c3Q9MCk8YnI+YGBgPGJyPjwvZGl2PndpbGwgcGxvdCB0aGUgdHJlZSB3aXRoIHRoZSBoZWF0\r\nbWFwLjxicj48ZGl2PjxkaXY+PGRpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5gYGByPGJyPmdo\r\nZWF0bWFwKEJvb20sbW9kX21hdCxvZmZzZXQ9NSwgd2lkdGg9MC41LGNvbG5hbWVzX2FuZ2xlPS00\r\nNSxoanVzdD0wKStzY2FsZV9jb2xvcl9tYW51YWwodmFsdWVzID0gYyhjb2xvcl9wYWxldHRlLCBi\r\ncmVha3M9bGFiZWxfdGV4dCkpPGJyPmBgYDxicj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5Zb3UgY29kZSB3aWxs\r\nIHByb2R1Y2UgaWRlbnRpY2FsIGZpZ3VyZSAobGVmdCBzaWRlIG9mIHRoZSBzY3JlZW5zaG90IGJl\r\nbG93KSBhcyBgc2NhbGVfY29sb3JfbWFudWFsYCB3aWxsIGJlIGlnbm9yZWQuPGJyPjxicj48YnI+\r\nQWN0dWFsbHksIHlvdSBwdXQgdGhlIGApYCBpbiB3cm9uZyBwbGFjZSBpbiBgc2NhbGVfY29sb3Jf\r\nbWFudWFsKHZhbHVlcyA9IGMoY29sb3JfcGFsZXR0ZSwgYnJlYWtzPWxhYmVsX3RleHQpKWAuPGJy\r\nPjxicj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5Zb3UgbmVlZCB0byB1c2UgYHNjYWxlX2ZpbGxfbWFudWFsYC4g\r\nQXMgc2hvd2VkIGJlbG93IG9uIHRoZSBzY3JlZW5zaG90LCB1c2luZyBgK3NjYWxlX2ZpbGxfbWFu\r\ndWFsYCB3aWxsIHRocm93IGVycm9yIGFzIHlvdXIgaW5wdXQgbWF0cml4IGlzIGNvbnRpbnVvdXMg\r\ndmFsdWUgd2hpbGUgeW91IGFyZSB0cnkgdG8gc2V0IGNvbG9yIGFzIGRpc2NyZXRlIHZhbHV